        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 170,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:35:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115053,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 170,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:35:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115054,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 170,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "<p>Chondroblastomas predominantly involve the epiphysis of long bones. When occurring in the head and neck, chondroblastomas are located mainly around the temporomandibular joint and the squamous part of the temporal bone {15875910; 21504272}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-12-19T14:25:36"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115055,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 170,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The most frequent clinical symptom is pain. Hearing loss, tinnitus, and vertigo may be present when tumours are located in the temporal bone, and trismus may be present if tumours are around the temporomandibular joint {15875910; 20614285}.</p>\r\n<h5>Imaging</h5>\r\n<p>Chondroblastomas of the temporal bone have a well-demarcated, lobulated, radiolucent appearance with foci of calcifications {15875910}. Cystic haemorrhagic degeneration may produce aneurysmal bone cyst&ndash;like changes with fluid levels on MRI {6470260; 10471886}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:35:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115056,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 170,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Chondroblastomas of the head and neck region are rare, with about 100&nbsp;cases reported in the literature {32603862}. Although most chondroblastomas occur in the second decade of life, patients with skull tumours are slightly older, presenting in their third or fourth decade of life {20614285}. A slight male predominance (M:F&nbsp;ratio: 1.3:1) has been reported for temporal chondroblastomas {32603862}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:35:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115057,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 170,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:35:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115058,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 170,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>H3-3A</em> and <em>H3-3B</em> mutations drive chondroblastoma, with the <em>H3-3B</em>:c.110A&gt;T p.K37M (K36M) mutation being most common {24162739; 27174990; 33779999}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:35:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115059,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 170,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Chondroblastomas are well-defined lesions with a thin sclerotic rim and a soft to gritty consistency. Haemorrhagic areas may be present.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:35:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115060,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 170,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumour cells are uniform, eosinophilic, and polygonal, with well-defined borders and nuclear grooves. The cells are intermingled with an amorphous eosinophilic matrix with osteoclast-like giant cells and varying amounts of chicken-wire calcification {5051664; 14880556}. Cystic haemorrhagic degeneration is frequent. Tumours harbouring mutations in <em>H3-3A</em> or <em>H3-3B</em> resulting in the expression of H3 p.K37M (K36M) mutant protein, show consistent nuclear immunoreactivity with a mutant-specific antibody K36M {26844533; 33779999}.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>The differential diagnosis includes aneurysmal bone cyst, clear cell chondrosarcoma, chondromyxoid fibroma, and Langerhans cell histiocytosis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:35:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115061,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 170,
        "headingId": 587,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:35:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 758,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 588,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115062,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 170,
        "headingId": 588,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Detection of the <em>H3-3B</em>:c.110A&gt;T p.K37M (K36M) mutation is highly specific for chondroblastoma {26457357; 33779999} and may be useful in selected cases.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:35:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 761,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 591,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115063,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 170,
        "headingId": 591,
        "headingText": "<p><em>Essential:</em> sheets of chondroblasts; scattered osteoclasts; eosinophilic chondroid matrix.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> a fine network of chicken-wire calcification; histone H3 mutation or H3 p.K37M (K36M) immunopositivity (in selected cases).</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-10T17:56:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 759,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 589,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115064,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 170,
        "headingId": 589,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:35:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 760,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 590,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115065,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 170,
        "headingId": 590,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>As many as 50% of cases recur. Metastasis has been reported only rarely (&lt;&nbsp;1% of cases) {3604981}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:35:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]